-- The error code and the message of every wrong option: 508 of them.
--
-- Generated by `python3 scripts/generate_bank_migration.py --retag --version 14` from
-- content/bank/*.json, and checked by `python3 content/render.py --check`.
--
-- Why a migration rather than an edit to V13: V13 is applied in every environment that has run it,
-- and Flyway records its checksum, so editing it fails validation on the next start. V13 also only
-- ever set `feedback`; the codes it left alone were the ones that turned out not to name the errors
-- they sat beside. Reading the options against the register found two kinds of mistake - a code
-- chosen for its family resemblance rather than its stated mechanism (4 x 3 + 1 on GRPH-ADD-NOT-TIMES,
-- which is about adding where x is multiplied), and codes used as buckets by options that had no
-- home in the register at all. Both are fixed in the bank; this applies the same fix to the loaded
-- bank of every database, so seed content and deployed content agree.
--
-- Every wrong option of the 180 questions is written here, rather than only the ones that
-- changed, so the statement of what the bank says is in one place and cannot drift from what the
-- files say. It is also idempotent: running it twice leaves the same rows.

